  "_readme": "Cabbageland paper world. Coordinates are in units of the 1983 × 793 panorama (x right, y down). Geometry (what is cut, where the water is) is measured on the day art and shared by every variant, so day and night pieces line up exactly. Edit, then run ./rebuild.sh; the site reads layers/layers.js. pieces are back-to-front. cut.subject = Vision subject-lift inside [x,y,w,h]; cut.within / cut.minus trim with a polygon; cut.polygon cuts by hand (dropSky keeps only the tree's own silhouette); cut.from takes the pixels from an extra source (the signs). keepUnder = leave the art under the piece instead of refilling it. pivot = hinge; parent = moves with another piece; spot = the place it belongs to (hover, click, room); kick = can be poked on its own.",
